  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 6.2. Increased capacity of Member States to strengthen policies and strategies to promote and ensure equal opportunities, participation and treatment between women and men, including equal remuneration for work of equal value</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gender Equality and Women&apos;s Empowerment Act was adopted in December 2022. The Act provides for equal pay (for work of persons with equal skills, competence, expertise and knowledge) (article 5). Furthermore, the Employment Act was adopted in May 2023 and provides, equal remuneration for men and women workers for work of equal value (article 18). Several meetings were held with the Government in 2022 on a memorandum on the draft Employment Act which was elaborated by ILO and shared with the Government of Sierra Leone in December 2018.  During these meetings specific questions on legislative changes discussed. The tripartite committee on labour reform considered the recommendations in the ILO&apos;s technical memorandum of 2018, as well as the comments and discussions in 2022. The relevant changes have now become effective in the above-mentioned Acts.</narrative>
   </description>
